// Minimal deterministic ReLico smoke-test model.
//
// A single actor re-arms itself once per time unit, carrying a constant
// payload:
//
//   constructor --after(1)--> tick --after(1)--> tick --after(1)--> ...
//
// Two properties make it the right shape for the artifact smoke test:
//
//   * It is deadlock-free. There is always exactly one future event (the next
//     tick), so the DTR model checker's deadlock-freedom / no-deadline-missed
//     property is satisfied rather than reporting a terminal deadlock state.
//   * Its state space is finite. The payload is a constant (1) and the single
//     state variable only ever stores that constant, so the model checker does
//     not diverge and no message queue overflows.
//
// Because each tick is scheduled `after(1)` (one logical millisecond), logical
// time advances by one unit per tick. The generated Lingua Franca program is
// run under a 5 msec logical-time bound, so it terminates on its own after a
// handful of ticks -- exactly what the runtime / example-execution gate needs.
//
// It sits well inside the supported (general) fragment: one reactive class,
// integer-valued message server, asynchronous self-send, constant delay, no
// priorities, no dynamic creation, no unbounded recurrence, no unbounded state.
//
// This model is intentionally tiny and is NOT part of the benchmark corpus or
// the translator fixture set; it exists solely so a reviewer's first command,
// ./smoke-test.sh, can exercise the whole verified pipeline end to end in a
// few seconds.
reactiveclass Ticker(10) {
    statevars {
        int last;
    }
    Ticker() {
        last = 0;
        self.tick(1) after(1);
    }
    msgsrv tick(int n) {
        last = n;
        self.tick(n) after(1);
    }
}
main {
    Ticker ticker():();
}
